HISTORY.

definition: def"
Query accepted CE-OS transitions by repository structure.

CE-OS owns exactly one semantic History ledger at repository root:
history.qps.

History is not current-system documentation. The applicable _index.qps
describes current truth and usage. History records accepted completed
transitions and their provenance.

The ledger may grow arbitrarily large because normal access is structural
query rather than linear human inspection.
";

storage: (
ledger- "history.qps";
location- "repository root only";
local_ledgers- false;
model- "accepted semantic transition entries";
);

entry_association: (
timestamp- "Save records the machine acceptance timestamp";
scope- "Each accepted entry records one or more repository paths associated with the work";
source_checklist- "Each accepted entry records the Checklist from which the completed task was accepted";
);

query: (
command- "qps history <path>";
source- "Parse the single repository-root history.qps ledger";
selection- "Return accepted entries whose authored scope associates them with the requested repository path";
scale- "Ledger length does not change the query model; structural association determines relevance";
);

authority: (
current_truth- "_index.qps";
unfinished_work- "checklist.qps";
accepted_transitions- "history.qps";
);
